<title>FRANCE: Lafarge links with Etex in Latin America.</title>
<headline>Lafarge links with Etex in Latin America.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French building materials group Lafarge said on Monday it and Etex Group had reached a cross-shareholding agreement with a view to developing the plaster market in Latin America together.</p>
<p>Lafarge said in a statement Lafarge Platres International would take a 40 percent stake in two Etex companies, Romeral in Chile and Durlock in Argentina.</p>
<p>In turn, Etex Group will take a 40 percent stake in Lafarge Gypsum in Brazil.</p>
<p>Lafarge would invest a net 150 million francs in the venture, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
